The enum parameters of the ``KeysightB1517A`` and ``KeysightB1520A`` modules of the Keysight
B1500, such as ``sweep_mode``, ``measurement_mode`` and ``impedance_model``, are now annotated
with their enum type, e.g. ``Parameter[constants.SweepMode, Self]``, and
``KeysightB1517A.time_axis`` as a numpy array. The parameters of the Keysight B220x and the
``phase`` of the ``AgilentE8257D`` and ``AgilentE8267C`` (``float``, in degrees) are annotated
as well. The ``post_sweep_voltage_val`` argument of ``KeysightB1517A.setup_staircase_sweep`` is
now typed as ``constants.WM.Post``, the enum used by the B1517A sweep, instead of
``constants.WMDCV.Post``, which belongs to the B1520A CV sweep. Both have the same values, so
existing calls keep working.

Parameters of the Keysight 344xxA DMMs and 33XXX waveform generators that can also be set to
SCPI keywords such as ``"MIN"``, ``"MAX"``, ``"DEF"`` or ``"INF"``, e.g.
``Keysight344xxASample.timer``, are annotated as ``Parameter[float | str, Self]`` (or
``int | str`` for counts). Getting them always returns a number, but the cached value is the
string that was set until the parameter is read again, as now explained in their docstrings.
